messages:   20%|##        | 41/204 [02:08<03:25,  1.26s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNo students who work in the library are from the computer science department. All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library. All students who take the database course are from the computer science department. All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course. All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David. James is a student working in the lab. Jack neither has a part-time job offered by the university nor works in the lab.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? James has a part-time job offered by the university.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "James has a part-time job offered by the university" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given information, let\'s analyze the context step by step:.\n\n1.**No students who work in the library are from the computer science department.**.\n   - This means that if someone works in the library, they cannot be from the computer science department.\n\n2.**All students who have part-time jobs offered by the university are students who work in the library.**.\n   - This implies that if a student has a part-time job offered by the university, they must be working in the library.\n\n3.**All students who take the database course are from the computer science department.**.\n   - This indicates that if a student takes the database course, they must be from the computer science department.\n\n4.**All students instructed by professor David are taking the database course.**.\n   - This means that if a student is instructed by professor David, they must be taking the database course.\n\n5.**All students working in the lab are instructed by professor David.**.\n   - This implies that if a student is working in the lab, they must be instructed by professor David.\n\n6.**James is a student working in the lab.**.\n   - This tells us that James is working in the lab.\n\nJack both has a part-time job offered by the university and works in the lab.\n- This implies that Jack has a part-time job offered by the university and works in the lab.\n\nNow, let\'s apply these rules to determine the status of James:\n\n- Since James is not working in the lab (rule 6), he must not be instructed by professor David (rule 5).\n- As James is not instructed by professor David, he must not be taking the database course (rule 4).\n- Since James is not taking the database course, he must not be from the computer science department (rule 3).\n- However, since James is not working in the lab, he must be from the computer science department (rule 1).\n\nThis creates a contradiction because James cannot be both from the computer science department and not from the computer science department simultaneously. Therefore, the statement "James has a part-time job offered by the university" is uncertain based on the given information.\n</think>.\n<answer>\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
