ely to have grown up in a health-conscious childhood home.\n\n4.**If people have good relationships with their parents, then they fulfill their nutritional daily intakes.**.\n   - This means that if someone has a good relationship with their parents, they are likely to fulfill their nutritional daily intakes.\n\n5.**If people have good relationships with their parents, then they do not eat salads regularly.**.\n   - This suggests that if someone has a good relationship with their parents, they are unlikely to eat salads regularly.\n\n6.**If people visit the gym at least once a day, then they always fulfill their daily nutritional intakes.**.\n   - This implies that if someone visits the gym at least once a day, they are likely to fulfill their daily nutritional intakes.\n\n7.**It is either both true that Taylor grew up in a health-conscious childhood home and she has a good relationship with her parents, or it is true that Taylor neither grew up in a health-conscious childhood home nor has a good relationship with her parents.**.\n   - This provides two possible scenarios for Taylor: either she grew up in a health-conscious childhood home and has a good relationship with her parents, or she did not grow up in a health-conscious childhood home and does not have a good relationship with her parents.\n\nNow, let\'s consider the implications of these scenarios for Taylor\'s salad eating habits:.\n\n- **Scenario 1: Taylor grew up in a health-conscious childhood home and has a good relationship with her parents.**.Given the analysis, the most logical conclusion is that Taylor does not eat salads regularly based on the information provided. Therefore, the correct answer is:\n\n**B) False**.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
